I'll never be free.

278
00:13:06,560 --> 00:13:10,840
I assumed those were the cards fate had dealt me.

279
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:13,780
It seemed hopeless, so I gave up.

280
00:13:16,920 --> 00:13:17,480
But...

281
00:13:17,480 --> 00:13:25,260
One day I realized being stuck there wasn't my fate after all.

282
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:28,420
I'd simply lacked the courage to change.

283
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:34,940
I left the Forest of Witches and chose life with the Black Bulls instead.

284
00:13:35,760 --> 00:13:37,420
And it was the right choice.

285
00:13:38,160 --> 00:13:40,760
We hold the threads of fate in our own hands.

286
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:43,200
And it's our choice what to do with them.

287
00:13:43,520 --> 00:13:45,440
Asuka! I'll pull you back in!

288
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:47,020
Just trust me and go!

289
00:13:47,200 --> 00:13:49,200
DITRINESSA, I'M COUNTING ON YOU!

290
00:13:53,360 --> 00:13:55,520
You ridiculous little fool!

291
00:13:55,520 --> 00:13:59,980
Take it easy, you two.

292
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,120
We don't want to go faster than we can handle.

293
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:04,860
This is the problem with passionate people.

294
00:14:05,360 --> 00:14:07,860
Much safer to be motivationally challenged like me.

295
00:14:09,240 --> 00:14:09,700
Fenril.

296
00:14:12,120 --> 00:14:15,020
Why are you wielding your magic so ineffectually?

297
00:14:15,020 --> 00:14:20,900
For generations, House Vod has used offensive spatial magic.

298
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:23,580
And it has served us well as magic knights.

299
00:14:23,880 --> 00:14:25,980
What use would that spell be in battle?

300
00:14:27,840 --> 00:14:28,520
But...

301
00:14:28,520 --> 00:14:31,420
I don't want to hurt anybody or get hurt.

302
00:14:32,100 --> 00:14:33,240
That sounds scary.

303
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:34,920
Gutless weakling.

304
00:14:34,920 --> 00:14:45,320
My, just look at how much of that column you shaved off.

305
00:14:45,700 --> 00:14:47,240
You're amazing, Lungris.

306
00:14:47,460 --> 00:14:48,920
An absolute genius.

307
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:50,160
Don't worry.

308
00:14:50,340 --> 00:14:52,340
We'll have someone fix whatever you've broken.

309
00:14:52,680 --> 00:14:54,080
You just keep practicing.

310
00:14:54,560 --> 00:14:56,420
We'll take care of everything, dear.

311
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:57,760
Honestly, Fenril.

312
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:00,900
Aren't you ashamed to be shown up by your younger brother?

313
00:15:00,900 --> 00:15:10,060
You're brothers.

314
00:15:10,580 --> 00:15:12,760
How could there be such a difference in your abilities?

315
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,560
Why, just look at Lungris.

316
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:19,080
He's already been made vice-captain of the Golden Dawn.

317
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:20,680
And what have you accomplished?

318
00:15:21,060 --> 00:15:23,480
You're nothing but a pack mule for the Black Bulls.

319
00:15:23,760 --> 00:15:25,720
The worst magic knight squad there is.

320
00:15:26,400 --> 00:15:29,240
Lungris will be taking over as head of House Vod.

321
00:15:29,240 --> 00:15:32,400
I trust you don't object.

322
00:15:33,600 --> 00:15:35,080
No, of course not.

323
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:37,900
I was just thinking it'd be a huge responsibility.

324
00:15:38,500 --> 00:15:40,020
Take good care of the place, Lungris.

325
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:43,360
I don't need you to tell me how to handle my affairs.

326
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:45,540
You're a disgrace to our house.

327
00:15:46,700 --> 00:15:49,180
Uh, yeah, I guess you're right.

328
00:15:49,720 --> 00:15:52,520
But hey, at least the girls really like my pretty face.

329
00:15:52,520 --> 00:15:58,320
I ran away from my father, my brother, my home, from reality.

330
00:15:58,940 --> 00:15:59,860
Hello there.

331
00:16:00,020 --> 00:16:01,820
You ladies sure are looking lovely.

332
00:16:02,480 --> 00:16:03,480
Wanna go grab a drink?

333
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,720
I know a nice cafe not far from here.

334
00:16:07,940 --> 00:16:13,620
I've got to say, darling, if you're as sweet as you are beautiful, I don't think we'll be ordering any dessert.

335
00:16:13,620 --> 00:16:18,080
And then, I met you, Asta.

336
00:16:18,740 --> 00:16:20,600
A boy utterly without magic.

337
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:22,160
Not too little.

338
00:16:22,660 --> 00:16:23,720
None at all.

339
00:16:24,380 --> 00:16:30,600
Instead of running from the fact that you couldn't cast a single spell, you faced it head-on and fought without ever giving up.

340
00:16:31,640 --> 00:16:34,840
True, I can't hope to best my brother as I am now.

341
00:16:35,600 --> 00:16:37,920
But, Yami?

342
00:16:38,420 --> 00:16:38,900
What?

343
00:16:38,900 --> 00:16:43,620
It's just that, why'd you let me join your squad, knowing I'm not much of a fighter?

344
00:16:44,420 --> 00:16:46,580
Figured you'd come in handy as a chauffeur.

345
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:50,280
Yeah, I guess that makes sense.

346
00:16:50,520 --> 00:16:53,760
I mean, it's not like my spells are good for taking down enemies or anything.

347
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:03,580
Maybe not, but you probably got your own way of fighting, don't you?

348
00:17:03,580 --> 00:17:03,980
Huh?

349
00:17:03,980 --> 00:17:09,380
There's a lot more to battle than just taking down enemies, you know.

350
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:12,340
Is it possible?

351
00:17:13,200 --> 00:17:14,600
My own way of fighting?

352
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:18,640
I know I'll never be the strongest mage.

353
00:17:20,240 --> 00:17:23,700
But I'll do what I can to make the Black Bulls the strongest squad.

354
00:17:24,400 --> 00:17:26,360
I stepped away from my own fight.

355
00:17:26,360 --> 00:17:29,480
And when I did, there were words I couldn't say anymore.

356
00:17:30,260 --> 00:17:31,680
But I can say them now.

357
00:17:32,600 --> 00:17:33,080
Asta!

358
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,720
I swear I won't mess this up!

359
00:17:36,060 --> 00:17:37,920
Please, just trust me, okay?

360
00:17:38,340 --> 00:17:39,340
Too late, Mineral!

361
00:17:39,580 --> 00:17:41,260
I already trust you completely!

362
00:17:41,260 --> 00:17:49,240
I'm impressed you aren't half bad.

363
00:17:50,240 --> 00:17:52,200
But you'll be at your limit soon.

364
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:55,620
If even one of you slips up, you'll be dead.

365
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:57,660
And you'll take the other two with you.

366
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:01,380
How long do you think you can actually keep going?

367
00:18:01,860 --> 00:18:02,680
Shut up!

368
00:18:02,860 --> 00:18:04,080
You really don't get it!

369
00:18:04,080 --> 00:18:07,080
We'll keep fighting like this for as long as we have to!

370
00:18:07,080 --> 00:18:11,320
Asta said he trusts me completely.

371
00:18:12,040 --> 00:18:13,560
And I guess it has to be true.

372
00:18:14,240 --> 00:18:18,320
Because how else could we possibly be pulling off this ridiculous method of fighting?

373
00:18:18,860 --> 00:18:19,240
Really?

374
00:18:19,740 --> 00:18:22,060
How can you so easily put your life in our hands?

375
00:18:22,700 --> 00:18:24,720
A drunken, lush, and a superficial slacker.

376
00:18:25,340 --> 00:18:28,360
Still, whatever made you believe in us...

377
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:30,160
We won't betray your trust!

378
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:33,640
Well done.

379
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:36,060
Your ability to focus is commendable.

380
00:18:36,060 --> 00:18:39,660
Although, how is your magic holding out?

381
00:18:39,960 --> 00:18:42,340
You'll be scraping the bottom of the barrel soon.

382
00:18:42,800 --> 00:18:44,720
Absolute amount of power.

383
00:18:45,160 --> 00:18:49,840
That is the definitive difference between my kind and yours, you fragile little insects.

384
00:18:50,700 --> 00:18:54,700
He may be full of himself, but unfortunately he's not wrong.

385
00:18:55,120 --> 00:18:56,720
My portals are starting to shrink.

386
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,000
My threads?

387
00:18:58,640 --> 00:18:59,580
They're screaming.

388
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:02,760
With my magic running out, they could snap any minute.

389
00:19:02,760 --> 00:19:05,820
I trust you two and we're gonna win!

390
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:14,880
It's not just two.

391
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:18,520
Looks like we made it in time.

392
00:19:18,700 --> 00:19:19,320
Oh yeah.

393
00:19:19,320 --> 00:19:23,440
Ghost?

394
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:25,240
Charmy!

395
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:27,060
And...

396
00:19:27,060 --> 00:19:29,000
That's grey.

397
00:19:29,660 --> 00:19:33,300
And this might sound like a terrible joke, but that's actually what she looks like.

398
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:34,120
What?

399
00:19:34,120 --> 00:19:34,420
What?

400
00:19:35,700 --> 00:19:37,880
Please, stop looking at me!

401
00:19:38,600 --> 00:19:39,940
Save all that for later.

402
00:19:39,940 --> 00:19:42,100
Right now, take this.

403
00:19:42,420 --> 00:19:44,440
With all the magic power I can muster.

404
00:19:45,500 --> 00:19:46,280
Mirror magic?

405
00:19:47,480 --> 00:19:48,540
Reflect refrain!

406
00:19:51,260 --> 00:19:52,960
What are you playing at?

407
00:19:53,080 --> 00:19:55,880
You think with enough blasts one has to land?

408
00:19:56,100 --> 00:19:57,960
I think you're right where I want you to be.

409
00:19:58,340 --> 00:19:59,240
Now, Five Head.

410
00:20:00,120 --> 00:20:01,640
Cotton creation magic!

411
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:06,260
Strike of a sleeping sheep!

412
